      "desc": "The insurer distributes claim cheques at a programme in Chattogram as part of efforts to expedite settlements.",
      "content": "Popular Life Insurance pays Tk9.68cr in claims to Chattogram customers | The Business Standard Popular Life Insurance pays Tk9.68cr in claims to Chattogram customers Last modified: 04 October, 2026, 06:22 pm Tk720cr land compensation trapped in Chattogram litigation maze Month-long breast cancer awareness campaign begins in Ctg 3 women among 7 detained in Ctg over food distribution marking Hasina's birthday Two groups clash over control of illegal drug trade in Ctg's Bakalia, 15 arrested Coast Guard seizes 48 tonnes of urea fertiliser, arrests 3 over smuggling attempt The insurer distributes claim cheques at a programme in Chattogram as part of efforts to expedite settlements. Last modified: 04 October, 2026, 06:22 pm Popular Life Insurance PLC representatives hand over an insurance claim cheque to a customer at a programme at the Engineers Institution auditorium in Chattogram on 3 October 2026. Photo: Courtesy Popular Life Insurance PLC has distributed insurance claim cheques worth Tk9.68 crore among customers in the Chattogram region as part of its efforts to expedite claim settlements. The cheques were handed over at a programme held at the Engineers Institution auditorium in Chattogram yesterday (3 October), according to a press release. Mohammad Zahirul Islam Chowdhury Rinku, chairman of Popular Life Insurance, attended the event as the chief guest, while BM Yusuf Ali, managing director and CEO of the company and president of the Bangladesh Insurance Forum, chaired the programme. Keep updated, follow The Business Standard's Google news channel Speaking at the event, Rinku stressed the need for prompt and proper settlement of insurance claims, saying honesty, hard work and professionalism are essential to winning customer confidence. \"By ensuring customer satisfaction and settling insurance claims quickly and properly, our collective efforts will help establish Popular Life as a pioneer in Bangladesh's insurance sector,\" he said. Former chairman and entrepreneur director Amir Humayun Mahmud Chowdhury, who attended the event as a special guest, said insurance plays an important role in providing financial security against uncertainties in life. He stressed the need for transparency, accountability and timely claim settlements to maintain customer trust in the insurance sector. BM Yusuf Ali said insurance provides financial protection against an uncertain future and that Popular Life has been working to ensure transparency, accountability and timely settlement of customer claims. \"The handover of these cheques today is a practical reflection of our responsibility towards our customers,\" he said. Additional managing director BM Shawkat Ali, additional managing director and company secretary Mehtas Helal Kabir, senior deputy managing director Syed Mehtahar Hossain, deputy managing director Md Khalilur Rahman Sikdar, executive director Sazzad Mahmud Kishore, project director Md Mahbubur Rahman and other senior officials also spoke at the programme. Customers who received the claim cheques expressed satisfaction with the payments. While most comments will be posted if they are on-topic and not abusive, moderation decisions are subjective. Published comments are readers’ own views and The Business Standard does not endorse any of the readers’ comments. IMF conditions unacceptable, we will raise funds from our own market: Finance minister Nasiruddin Patwary attacked, car vandalised at Lalon Shah shrine in Kushtia LPG price hike adds to consumer woes amid supply shortages Major cracks, cave-ins raise safety concerns on Dhaka Bypass in Sonargaon Govt plans $300m fast-track project to turn Chattogram airport into regional air hub PM orders faster progress on inner circular road project to ease Dhaka traffic Why private sector turns away from foreign loans India recommends anti-dumping duty on PET film imports from Bangladesh 12kg LPG cylinder price rises by Tk252 to Tk1,837 Tk720cr land compensation trapped in C