      "title": "A replica Oval Office near the White House just got a new Trump makeover. Gold flourishes abound",
      "desc": "",
      "content": "Oval Office replica gets a gold makeover in Trump's second term - Action News Jax A replica Oval Office near the White House just got a new Trump makeover. Gold flourishes abound WASHINGTON — It’s glitzier. And there’s way more gold. Gleaming vases, golden-hued swirling onlays, two dozen portraits in heavy gilded frames and knickknacks crowding nearly every available surface: the same rococo flourishes that Trump has installed in the world’s most famous workspace have been recreated down to each wall appliqué in a museum just up Pennsylvania Avenue from the White House. “As political as the Oval Office is, it really is also the office of the American people,” said Luke Boorady, managing director of The People’s House: A White House Experience. “And we want visitors who come here to feel more connected to this space.” Public tours of the White House do not include the West Wing. So the White House Historical Association set about recreating the Oval Office, opening the exhibit in September 2024. It is the same size as the real one, and visitors often marvel at how small it feels. A team of specialized designers has been making over the exhibit, visiting Trump's Oval Office while the Republican president was away. Experts in North Carolina worked to recreate Trump's many wall appliqués, while one from Indianapolis handled 3D scanning and printing of other specialized objects. California frame-makers did carving by hand for the gold frames of Trump's chosen 24 portraits, and teams from Canada and Virginia worked on replicas of vases and other tabletop pieces, Boorady said. There are also two mirrors and a copy of the Declaration of Independence, just like in Trump's actual office. The president has molded the White House in his own image A real estate developer before he became a politician, Trump has to his extravagant tastes as part of his push to what he would miss most about the White House after he leaves, Trump said, \"This beautiful room that nobody should be allowed to rip down. The Oval Office.\" He said he had asked his chief of staff to make his altered office \"a federal landmark.\" In addition to filling the Oval Office with bling, Trump paved over the lawn near the Rose Garden to build a along the colonnade between the White House residence and the West Wing. He erected towering flagpoles on the North and South lawns, renovated the Palm Room and the bathroom that is part of the famous Lincoln Bedroom and ordered restoration work of the that he is building after ordering that the . \"It relaxes me, actually,\" the president said about the ballroom project during an unrelated event last week. Trump's sense of ownership of the White House is now such that while recently defending his attempt to ban CNN, MS Now and Politico from its grounds , the president had a momentary slip of the tongue. \"I don't have to let them into my — into the people's house,\" he said. A replica of Trump's first term Oval Office gets a makeover When the White House Historical Association first opened its Oval Office duplicate, it mirrored Democratic President Joe Biden's design. After the 2024 election, the association updated the exhibit to match Trump's first-term style. Last week, a crew of 25 people worked from early Monday through late Friday to get the second-term transformation ready, making the finishing touches on Saturday. Boorady said Biden was the first president to hang double layers of portraits over the Oval Office fireplace. Trump has expanded that all around the room, stacking the walls with portraits including those of George Washington, Andrew Jackson and Benjamin Franklin. In the real Oval Office, the colors are made more brilliant by using gilded gold leaf. In the replica, crews used a paint solution. Boorady said they did not use gold leaf to protect against chipping or other wear-and-tear from visitors moving through the area. Trump was once spotted using superglue to try to affix gold ornaments to the Oval Office fireplace, ac",
      "url": "https://www.actionnewsjax.com/news/politics/replica-oval-office/WCAN42MWMIY5JGAPFA6IL5OFAQ/",
      "image": "https://www.actionnewsjax.com/resizer/v2/Q2VCIRHZXQ3EHFOPDVNKXKTKLY.jpg?auth=6ce3ccc4f03e25280483dbf4a21462f4da4cb11267f851d1b6f6ae13dd0b4c1f&smart=true&width=6000&height=4000",
      "source": "actionnewsjax",
